Texture and buffer caches age, and collect garbage, while nothing is presented.
(ProsperoEden patches/eden/eden-67bada77-ns2-sw2-ps5.d 0036 cache-ticks-without-present and 0041
idle-tick-never-waits, adapted to Eglantine.)

The caches age by presented frames (RasterizerVulkan::TickFrame from the present path). A game can
render for minutes without presenting (Mario Kart World loads ~7 GiB of textures first), so at the
end of a command list (GPU::OnCommandListEnd, on the split's back when it runs) after 250 ms
without a present they age by time, once the host GPU has finished what was submitted before the
check: images retired by an age tick are destroyed a few ticks later. It never waits for the GPU
(GPU work can wait on guest work this thread has yet to process): it submits, notes the tick, and
ticks the caches at a later command list end once that tick is done. EDEN_IDLE_CACHE_TICK=0 ages
them by presents only.

